## Secret Letter's market claim as ADR-365 AC-8 measured it: Grubber's Market
## during the calm, the fourteen market rooms plus Commerce Street so the
## guarded east exit is tried, the twenty-six takeable wares, take and drop.
## The set is deliberately padded — the claim's predicate reads only where
## the player is — which is what the cone's finding is for. A test fixture
## only: the story is read beside it, never edited.

claims
  needs rooms: the Northwest Junction, the Grocery Stall, the Fruit Stall, the Eastern Junction, the Hat Stall, the Leather Stall, the Weaponsmith's Stall, the Exotic Gems Stall, the Herb Stall, the Rope Stall, the Candlemaker's Stall, the Pottery Stall, Outside the Silk Tent, Inside the Silk Tent, Commerce Street
  needs things: the banana, the pear, the kello fruit, the cluster of brambleberries, the orange, the lime, the loaf, the cheese, the strip of beef jerky, the riding reins, the harness, the stirrup, the plain scabbard, the belt, the knife, the herb jar, the length of rope, the tallow candle, the red wax candle, the blue wax candle, the green wax candle, the white wax candle, the clay pot, the clay urn, the clay jar, the clay bowl
  needs verbs: take, drop

  never Jack reaches Commerce Street while the market is calm
    the player is in Commerce Street
end claims
